      "date": "2026-05-15T12:43:00.000Z",
      "title": "A. K. Capital Services Limited to Report Q4, 2026 Results on May 20, 2026",
      "body": "A. K. Capital Services Limited announced that they will report Q4, 2026 results on May 20, 2026",
      "keyDevTypeId": "55",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "787a42cc-b255-4abe-b3a8-c184ef94cfeb",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-03-06T11:34:17.000Z",
      "title": "MD & Executive Director recently bought ₹2.8m worth of stock",
      "body": "On the 2nd of March, Atul Mittal bought around 2k shares on-market at roughly ₹1,519 per share. This transaction amounted to less than 1% of their direct individual holding at the time of the trade. This was the largest purchase by an insider in the last 3 months. Atul has been a buyer over the last 12 months, purchasing a net total of ₹104m worth in shares.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "1be2cb16-1add-43c1-9779-8bb69985a3d8",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-02-11T11:39:52.000Z",
      "title": "Dividend of ₹22.00 announced",
      "body": "Shareholders will receive a dividend of ₹22.00. Ex-date: 24th February 2026 Payment date: 6th March 2026 Dividend yield will be 3.2%, which is higher than the industry average of 1.3%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is covered by earnings (33% earnings payout ratio) but the company has no free cash flows available, indicating it may be using cash reserves or debt to pay the dividend. The dividend has increased by an average of 20% per year over the past 10 years and has been stable with no material reductions to payments, indicating a long track record of dividend growth and stability. Earnings per share has grown by 9.7% over the last 5 years. Unless this trend reverses, it should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f4d579d-897c-4852-9349-59146be9ed6a",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-02-09T00:05:11.000Z",
      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹37.92 (vs ₹25.00 in 3Q 2025)",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹37.92 (up from ₹25.00 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹1.35b (up 17% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹250.3m (up 52% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 19% (up from 14% in 3Q 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 3% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 51% per year, which means it is tracking significantly ahead of earnings growth.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "8c1545c1-13c7-40a4-9c58-77d7c1816507",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-02-07T11:17:00.000Z",
      "title": "A. K. Capital Services Limited Declares Second Interim Dividend for the Financial Year 2025-26",
      "body": "A. K. Capital Services Limited announced that the Board of Directors at their meeting held on February 7, 2026, has Declared 2nd Interim Dividend of INR 22/- per fully paid up equity share (face value of INR 10/- per equity share) for the financial year 2025-26 and fixed the Record Date as February 24, 2026 to determine the names of the equity shareholders of the Company who shall be entitled to receive Interim Dividend.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "46",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "818f4950-0e00-4792-bc52-ebec388e3933",
